+section('client-setup', 'Client setup', 'motherboard')
  p.
    A Client (#[code thub-client]) is a daemon on a lab machine. One #[strong instance] owns one DUT slot. A machine with
    several boards runs several instances (#[code dut0], #[code dut1], …), each with its own config file.
    Clients register themselves with the shared join key; there's no admin step.

  h3.h6 1. Install
  +code('Lab machine, as the user the Client should run as (via sudo)').
    # Node.js and HW tools (stlink-tools/openocd only for HW Clients)
    sudo apt install -y nodejs npm stlink-tools openocd usbutils
    # Docker: needed on SW Clients, and on HW Clients whose jobs use docker.
    # Install it BEFORE thub-client so the service gets the docker group.
    sudo apt install -y docker.io
    sudo npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-client
  p.small.
    This creates #[code ~/.config/thub/client.json] and #[code ~/var/lib/thub/client] for the user who ran
    #[code sudo], and installs the #[code thub-client@.service] systemd unit running as that user, with the
    #[code dialout], #[code plugdev] and #[code docker] groups. It also installs the root helpers that
    apply self-updates and scheduled reboots.

  h3.h6 2. Configure and start
  .row.g-3
    .col-md-6
      +code('SW Client — ~/.config/thub/client.json').
        {
          "coordinatorUrl": "#{coordinatorUrl}",
          "name": "lab-sw-01",
          "type": "sw",
          "labels": [],
          "groups": [],
          "joinKey": "&lt;the Coordinator's clientJoinKey>",
          "varDir": "/home/thub/var/lib/thub/client"
        }
    .col-md-6
      +code('HW Client — ~/.config/thub/client.json').
        {
          "coordinatorUrl": "#{coordinatorUrl}",
          "name": "lab-hw-01",
          "type": "hw",
          "labels": ["board:nucleo-f401re", "uart", "stlink"],
          "joinKey": "&lt;the Coordinator's clientJoinKey>",
          "varDir": "/home/thub/var/lib/thub/client",
          "hw-devices": {
            "stlinks": [{ "index": 1, "devpath": "3.3.4.3.1" }],
            "uarts":   [{ "index": 1, "devpath": "3.3.3.2", "baudRate": 115200 }],
            "usbs":    [{ "index": 1, "devpath": "3.2.4" }]
          }
        }
  +code('Start it and follow the log').
    sudo systemctl enable --now thub-client@client
    journalctl -u thub-client@client -f

  h3.h6 Config reference
  .table-responsive
    table.table.table-sm.small
      thead
        tr
          th Field
          th Required
          th Meaning
      tbody
        tr
          td: code coordinatorUrl
          td Yes
          td The Coordinator's #[code publicUrl].
        tr
          td: code type
          td Yes
          td #[code hw] (physical DUT) or #[code sw] (DUT image in Docker).
        tr
          td: code joinKey
          td Yes
          td Must equal the Coordinator's #[code clientJoinKey]. Or set #[code THUB_CLIENT_JOIN_KEY].
        tr
          td: code name
          td No
          td Runner name. Under systemd, the instance name (#[code thub-client@dut1] → #[code dut1]) is used unless an admin renames it on the dashboard.
        tr
          td: code labels
          td No
          td Matched against a job's #[code --board]/#[code --label]. Use #[code board:&lt;name>] for the board.
        tr
          td: code groups
          td No
          td The runner groups this Client belongs to. Set them on its runner card (Groups tab), which writes them here.
        tr
          td: code varDir
          td No
          td State directory: tokens, the client id, job workspaces, sockets. Keep the installer's default under systemd.
        tr
          td: code hw-devices.stlinks / uarts / usbs
          td HW
          td Up to 8 of each. An entry is a udev index #[code N] (→ #[code /dev/thub/dut&lt;N>-stlink|uart|usb]), a path, or an object with #[code index]/#[code path], #[code devpath] (USB port), #[code serial] (ST-Link) and #[code baudRate] (UART, default 115200).
        tr
          td: code heartbeatIntervalSec / longPollWaitSec
          td No
          td 10 s / 30 s by default.
        tr
          td: code clientId
          td No
          td An explicit identity UUID (or #[code THUB_CLIENT_ID]). Normally generated once and kept in #[code .client-id].
  p.small.
    SW Clients have no settings of their own: they run whatever DUT image a job brings (#[code --docker-image]).
    Admins can also edit an HW Client's devices from its runner card (#[strong ST-Link | UART | DUT USB]
    tabs). The tabs show the config the Client runs, as it reported it at its last start, or a saved
    change it hasn't applied yet. #[strong Connected USB devices → Import to config] fills them from the host's #[code lsusb].
    The card's #[strong Export] and #[strong Import] icons download a Client's config file (never its
    #[code joinKey]) and apply one to it. An older HW Client takes only the file's #[code hw-devices].
    There's no ST-Link serial field: the job's #[code --command] picks the probe
    (#[code $THUB_DUT_STLINK_&lt;n&gt;]), and the Client reads each serial from its udev symlink.

  h3.h6 Several DUT slots on one machine
  +code('One instance per slot').
    thub-client register --name dut1 --type hw    # creates ~/.config/thub/dut1.json, starts thub-client@dut1
    nano ~/.config/thub/dut1.json                 # set that slot's hw-devices
    sudo systemctl restart thub-client@dut1
    thub-client deregister --name dut1            # when the slot goes away

  h3.h6 Controlling a Client
  +code('As the Client\'s user (not with sudo)').
    thub-client status
    thub-client lock --reason "debugging I2C"     # BUSY (local): nothing gets scheduled here
    thub-client unlock
    thub-client restart
    thub-client --config ~/.config/thub/dut1.json status    # a specific instance
    thub-client udev --print                                # the udev rules this config generates
